WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:05.770
We'll protect this princess from 
the monsters that attack.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.610
That's the occult club's job here.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.430
For how long?

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.360
Until she completes her theory.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.540
And when will that be?

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.540
When she completes it.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.870
You're asking a lot, Pops.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.160
Who are you calling Pops?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.400
Well, you went and grew up all by yourself.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.670
Whoa, you're right!

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.710
Why?

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.510
Episode 16
"The Truth Nobody Knows"

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.720
What is this theory, anyway?

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.590
A way to save Earth.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.380
From re-evolution, though I 
guess you wouldn't get that.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.060
Nope, I don't.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:37.930
But...

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.010
Okay, if you say so.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.140
And who are we up against?

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.520
Kashima Sakura.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.900
Oh, her.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.050
Anyway, I want someone to 
stay by Kagari at all times.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.150
Oh, sorry.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:01:00.530
I just found it funny that Gaia and Guardian 
are going to protect the Key together.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.950
To save the planet, no less.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:04.830
Yeah. How exciting.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.670
Time to get right to work, huh?

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.770
I like a challenge.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.730
Did monsters show up?

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.340
Looks like it.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.270
I should give you these while 
I still have the chance.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.350
Sorry.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.850
I couldn't prepare anything 
too complicated, like guns.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.500
No problem.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.970
My main weapon is my body.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.400
All good.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.480
This will be easy.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.610
You protect Kagari with these guys, Kotori.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.380
Good boys.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.740
You're called Dima and Lyuba, huh?

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.490
This one's for you, President.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.140
Survey the battlefield with it.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.500
You got it.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.090
For Chihaya...

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:48.870
This should do.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.630
Why am I the odd one out?

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.460
Yoshino?

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.720
<i>Sorry. We were no match for them.</i>

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.890
No, you were a big help. Thanks.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.170
We'll save Earth.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.060
It's a huge job befitting 
the occult club's comeback.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.390
I'm counting on you all!

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.900
For some reason, this battle 
has me in high spirits.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.320
You don't understand why, Shizuru?

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.160
It's because you're 
fighting for your friends.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.720
I see.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.910
Right, that makes sense.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.360
Of course that'd make me really happy.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.670
Yeah, same here.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.280
<i>Here comes one.</i>

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.190
<i>Aim for the monster's legs, Kotori.</i>

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.100
Got it.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.670
Dima, Lyuba!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.320
Hit it hard, Chihaya!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.860
Aye aye!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>We're done here.</i>

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.900
<i>You're the last to finish, Kotarou.</i>

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.120
Roger that. Good work.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.220
Talk about some dependable friends.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.960
I'm glad you're all okay.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.100
Guess we took the first battle.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.360
That said, they were all way 
stronger than regular monsters.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.770
But of course, given we're 
up against Kashima Sakura...

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:44.370
We should expect her to keep sending ones 
that are equally strong, if not stronger.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:45.530
We can do this.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:45.870
Yeah.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.260
You sure are confident.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.000
Tea is served!

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.290
Kagari didn't get any.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.500
Make another cup, please.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.940
Allow me to be blunt.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.890
We haven't been able to 
see her for a while now.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.390
We can sense a powerful being 
nearby, but we can't see her.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:10.890
Oh...

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.770
Even here, Kagari has to be all alone?

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.520
This is quite the interesting theory.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.420
It shows the path the world 
and its life have taken.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.010
It starts off strong,

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.160
but peters out in the end.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.410
You can decipher it?

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.440
It kind of resembles the process 
for producing a monster.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.290
Though this is far more advanced, of course.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.290
So what exactly is that?

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.700
Researching the theory of life, huh?

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.400
So even the all-powerful 
Kagari has her limits.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.280
Yeah.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.210
Aurora isn't omnipotent.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.860
There's nothing it can do 
if the resources run out.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.180
Value the resources!

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:53.980
But the development of civilization 
requires consumption of resources.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.660
And it's too late to stop environmental 
destruction once the damage is done.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.440
Humans are so foolish.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.570
The final boss?!

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:07.200
The best option is to destroy civilization 
immediately every time it appears.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.950
She really is the final boss!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.190
Okay, then.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.830
Let's run some simulations on a copy.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.940
We can leave the early stages in auto mode.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.800
The Big Splash happens, and the 
leftover debris become the moon.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.950
It's like a game.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:27.890
All right, then.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.230
Take a crack at it.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.760
Leave it to me.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.360
I hold the fate of the foolish human 
race in the palms of my hands.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.850
Please don't get any strange ideas!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.310
Why'd you destroy it right off the bat?!

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:46.780
It wasn't my fault.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.490
I'll go next, then.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.770
It got destroyed again!

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.700
I never dreamed a demon would show 
up and devour the entire world!

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.500
Uh, you were the creator.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.500
Can I go next?

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.930
Why do you all immediately destroy Earth?!

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:13.580
Oh.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.270
Humanity came into existence 
while I was playing around.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.520
For real?!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.660
They've formed a civilization and a country.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.090
The country's splitting up!

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.760
We'd better cull some humans.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.190
It's scary how casually she says it.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.000
A huge empire has been created.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.480
It suddenly stopped making progress.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.760
They went on the defensive after it expanded.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.770
But the population is still growing.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.390
What?!

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.140
It's destroyed all of a sudden!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.000
Kotarou-kun, look at this!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.680
Is this the Key?

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.770
Why'd it end the world?

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:11.220
Probably because Earth's resources 
would've been extinguished eventually.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:15.220
Kotori, can you tell us anything 
you remember about Kagari?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.960
Only that legend says she's 
looking for fond memories.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.910
Fond memories?

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.040
For the planet?

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.470
Speaking of which, I wonder 
how it went during our time.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.620
We died out in the end each time,

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.330
but surely there were phases 
where things might've worked out.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:39.480
Yeah, several projects came up 
to stave off the impending doom.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.170
There were even plans to expand into space.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:45.230
But they all failed in the end.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.870
I see.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.390
<i>What were we lacking in 
order to save the planet?</i>

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.240
<i>In the world with the president,</i>

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.240
<i>the one with Shizuru,</i>

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.250
<i>the one with Chihaya,</i>

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.250
<i>the one with Lucia,</i>

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:08.000
<i>and Kotori's...</i>

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:11.510
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:12.910
<i>Wait.</i>

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>Wait a second.</i>

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:19.930
<i>What is this void that 
exists in every memory?</i>

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.120
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.740
<i>I always meet Kagari and 
nearly get killed by her.</i>

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.370
<i>Kotori saves me using her Druid powers,</i>

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.350
<i>and time stops for me.</i>

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.970
<i>I'm really much older than all of them,</i>

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.500
<i>and the time I spent in a coma, over a decade,</i>

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.060
<i>was the same in every world.</i>

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:13.530
<i>If that time was what we 
lacked to save the world,</i>

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.230
<i>that'd mean the root cause was 
that I got involved too late.</i>

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.460
What's up, Kagari?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.420
What's this?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.180
The branch worlds that had died out for sure

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:35.170
now have uncertain futures?

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:37.520
Great job.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.160
You did well.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:41.680
It's fine, Kagari.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.930
Better uncertain than certain doom.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.100
There's still hope that way.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.740
Oh, yeah.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.280
Can I write a message to commemorate this?

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.490
Humans do this all the time.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.860
I want to meet you someday.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:55.860
-Tennouji Kotarou

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:57.680
It's a bit corny, but whatever.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:06.000
There. It shouldn't affect the 
theory all the way over here.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:10.500
Kagari?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.240
Is this... a new theory?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.760
Why now?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.260
A new future?

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.040
Wow!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.200
All right! You did it, Kagari!

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:53.790
Kagari?

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.200
What's wrong?

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.300
You completed your theory, 
so why do you look so sad?

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.570
<i>Hey, the enemy's attacking! 
Their numbers are insane!</i>

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.570
So you noticed, Kashima Sakura.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.200
Kagari completed her research.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.150
But it looks like it'll take her some time

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.210
to put her completed theory into action.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.460
We're hopelessly outnumbered here, but...

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:38.350
Keeping Kagari safe is our highest priority.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.090
Got it?

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.720
We'll need to work out a strategy.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.720
I've enhanced Dima and Lyuba's 
mobility, so now we can

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.100
use them for guerrilla warfare.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:48.350
I'll just swing some logs around.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.730
I'll set up as many traps as possible.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.140
Guys...

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:54.750
<i>In the new world,</i>

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:58.400
<i>I bet I won't get to spend time 
with them as someone their age.</i>

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.570
<i>Since this is the end, I'll put on a show</i>

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.810
<i>with the strength I gained 
living a peaceful life.</i>

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.620
Yeah, this is how the occult club should be.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:17.130
Occult club, fight!

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.380
Yeah!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.380
Yeah...

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.240
Men!

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:25.140
Bare your fangs against those 
that dare defile us wolves' turf!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.540
Go to...

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.760
...hell!

00:12:30.590 --> 00:12:33.350
If it's for my friends, I can use 
this power I hate so much!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.810
Kotarou's counting on me.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.370
I'll give all I have.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.950
Dima, Lyuba... Go!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.250
Get down, Kotori!

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.020
Thanks, Chi-chan.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:04.760
No problem.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.260
Thank you too, President!

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.380
You're welcome.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.100
Now, then.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.370
Kashima Sakura...

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.580
I don't understand how you must've felt

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.190
to send this many monsters across worlds.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:27.430
A song?

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.400
Kagari...

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.000
Why, you!

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:45.830
Keep your filthy paws off my girl!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:53.520
<i>Tennouji.</i>

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.060
Yoshino?

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.320
What's up?

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:58.280
<i>The enemy sent reinforcements.</i>

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.820
<i>I lost all of my buddies.</i>

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.320
You did?

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:03.280
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.030
They all showed their rock star 
spirit until the very end.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.030
Yoshino.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.300
End of the line, huh?

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:41.900
Yeah, I've already...

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:50.350
Great job.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:53.890
I was... really happy.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.000
So, next time...

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:07.630
Kotarou...

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.250
For everything you've given us...

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:23.990
Forgive me for doing nothing 
but cause you trouble, Kotarou.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.190
Please beat her...

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:31.780
And...

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:38.500
Kotarou...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.460
In truth, I want to once more—

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.840
Protect her all the way.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:50.590
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.270
<i>It's time for me to go, too.</i>

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:53.050
Yoshino...

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:54.320
Tell me.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.550
Was I of any use at all?

00:15:57.190 --> 00:16:02.050
I only got to stay a loner 
because you rejected me.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:06.220
And I only got to be a trailblazer 
because I was a loner.

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.620
<i>Tell me in a language I can understand.</i>

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.950
I'm saying we're eternal rivals, Yoshino.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.450
Now that's what I call mach.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.080
I'm gonna go out in a blaze of glory,

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.140
because that's how I roll.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:23.570
This is the perfect last gig for me.

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.640
Isn't that right,

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:25.460
Kotarou?

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.560
Yeah, exactly.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:31.920
Give them hell,

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.090
Haruhiko.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.600
Goodbye, my brother!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.720
See you in the next life!

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.480
Yee-haw!

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:50.340
It begins.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:55.160
Aurora is rebuilding this 
fleeting world into a new one.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.230
You pieces of shit!

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.630
Why are you here,

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.260
Sakuya?!

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.700
In the nick of time...

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:17.660
Or so I'd like to say, but it 
seems I was a bit too late.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.580
I'm sorry, Chihaya-san.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:29.400
I took too long to unite my 
different selves and come here.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:33.400
This is no time to be 
spacing out, Slowtarou-kun.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:36.570
Your beloved sleeping 
beauty is in grave peril.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.490
You always get on my nerves.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.560
But...

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:50.840
Nobody could be more dependable 
at times like these.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.000
Indeed.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.130
I believe I'm stronger now 
than I was in any other world.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:26.750
I once told you that you were my fate.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.370
I don't remember stuff from that long ago.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:32.510
But you surpassed my destiny and repainted

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.630
what lay beyond it in your own colors.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:40.330
I couldn't have stood here and 
created new possibilities.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:43.120
We have the same abilities 
and share the same fate.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:45.890
So maybe it was because I'm a newer model.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:53.020
The enemy seems hellbent on 
not giving us a moment's rest.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:57.830
Good grief.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:06.290
I think I depended on you in every world.

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.160
I'm counting on you, bro.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.840
Leave it to me,

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.290
bro.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:21.340
Sakuya, don't tell me...

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:27.250
I took too long to unite my 
different selves and come here.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:32.100
You linked every branch-world Sakuya

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.900
to this realm?

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:42.410
You shut the door on your 
fate in order to stand here?

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.100
You moron.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.270
I'll remember you.

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.420
The me right here will, if no one else.

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:58.530
It's my turn now.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.550
Hit that final switch!

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.370
<i>Farewell...</i>

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:37.760
<i>Farewell, Tennouji Kotarou...</i>

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.380
<i>Thank you, Tennouji Kotarou...</i>

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.880
<i>For caring about me when I'm so selfish.</i>

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.350
It's fine.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:49.260
Love is much more than that.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:53.100
<i>You said you want to meet me.</i>

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.770
<i>But we'll never see each other again.</i>

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.720
Wait, Kagari!

00:20:57.720 --> 00:20:59.520
Aren't you coming with us?

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:01.380
The moon?

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:04.080
Are we going to start over on the moon?

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:06.660
It's so huge...

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.170
Huge?

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:14.560
I see.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:17.420
So we were on the moon all this time,

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.380
and that's the real Earth?

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.920
Earth was teeming with life,

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.170
but the moon only gave birth to Kagari.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:27.320
Kagari...

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:30.090
You used the remnants of 
Earth's Aurora on the moon,

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.780
where you were all alone,

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:34.180
and made a replica of Earth?

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:36.840
<i>It was an inexcusable act,</i>

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.720
<i>born from feelings I shouldn't have accepted.</i>

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.400
<i>I'll return what I took and 
go back to being nothing.</i>

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.900
Kagari... Kagari?

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:50.210
<i>With these memories, I can 
endure the loneliness.</i>

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:52.660
<i>That's all I ever wanted.</i>

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.660
Stop it, you idiot.

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:57.540
<i>Bon voyage, humanity.</i>

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:01.760
Kagari!

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:14.000
<i>Earth...</i>

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:16.290
<i>Our home.</i>

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:20.220
<i>Our faraway home planet.</i>

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:25.290
<i>A planet that fell into ruin, 
lost all its life, and died.</i>

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:29.720
<i>We have to start over.</i>

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:35.410
<i>But that Kagari won't be there.</i>

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:38.480
<i>I won't be there as I am now, either.</i>

00:22:42.830 --> 00:22:44.290
<i>All I can do is make a wish.</i>

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:49.270
<i>If anyone ever makes it to the heavens,</i>

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:54.160
<i>I hope they find the girl on the moon...</i>

00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:00.560
<i>From the very bottom of my heart.</i>

00:23:51.880 --> 00:23:55.780
<i>Now, in this new world...</i>

00:23:56.490 --> 00:24:00.000
Let's begin the cruel process of selection.
